---
import RedirectCode from '@/components/RedirectCode.astro'
import heroFed from './assets/images/hero-fed.png'

// 九月议息会议决议公布时间（新加坡时间）。如需调整，只改这一行。
const FOMC_AT = '2026-09-17T02:00:00+08:00'

// 构建时算出的初值，只作为 JS 未执行时的兜底，页面加载后由脚本立刻校正
const diffMs = Math.max(0, new Date(FOMC_AT).getTime() - Date.now())
const initDays = String(Math.floor(diffMs / 86400000))
const initHours = String(Math.floor(diffMs / 3600000) % 24).padStart(2, '0')
const initMins = String(Math.floor(diffMs / 60000) % 60).padStart(2, '0')
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-SG">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <title>The September Fed Meeting Just Became the One That Matters — A Singapore Investor's Countdown</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="US payrolls fell by 23,000 in July against a forecast of +83,000, and inflation still isn't beaten. The Fed has to pick which problem to make worse in September. Here's what to get straight before the decision, in Singapore hours."
    />

    <RedirectCode />

    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@400;500;600;700;800&family=Roboto+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />

    <style
      define:vars={{
        fedImg: `url(${heroFed.src})`,
      }}
    >
      :root {
        --night: #121826;
        --night-2: #0c111c;
        --slab: #1a2233;
        --stone: #eaecf1;
        --stone-d: #c2c8d6;
        --mut: #98a1b3;
        --dim: #6c7587;
        --glow: #e9b44c;
        --edge: rgba(234, 236, 241, 0.12);
        --wa: #25d366;
        --wa-d: #1bae52;
        --sans: 'Archivo', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
        --mono: 'Roboto Mono', ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace;
      }

      * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
      html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; scroll-behavior: smooth; }
      body {
        font-family: var(--sans);
        background: var(--night);
        color: var(--stone);
        line-height: 1.58;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
        overflow-x: hidden;
        padding-bottom: calc(84px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
      }
      img { display: block; max-width: 100%; }

      .wrap { width: 100%; padding-inline: 22px; }

      /* ---------- hero ---------- */
      .hero {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        min-height: 100svh;
        padding-top: calc(env(safe-area-inset-top) + 40px);
        padding-bottom: calc(104px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
        background-image:
          linear-gradient(184deg, rgba(12, 17, 28, 0.78) 0%, rgba(12, 17, 28, 0.5) 30%, rgba(12, 17, 28, 0.94) 88%),
          var(--fedImg);
        background-size: cover, auto 122%;
        background-position: center, 62% 30%;
        background-repeat: no-repeat;
      }
      .hero h1 {
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 9.2vw, 2.85rem);
        line-height: 1.09;
        letter-spacing: -0.028em;
        text-wrap: balance;
      }
      .hero h1 span { color: var(--glow); }
      .hero .lede {
        margin-top: 18px;
        font-size: 1.02rem;
        color: var(--mut);
        max-width: 44ch;
      }

      /* ---------- countdown ---------- */
      .count-label {
        margin-top: 34px;
        font-family: var(--mono);
        font-size: 0.68rem;
        font-weight: 500;
        letter-spacing: 0.16em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--stone-d);
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 11px;
      }
      .count-label::before {
        content: '';
        width: 7px;
        height: 7px;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background: var(--glow);
        box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px rgba(233, 180, 76, 0.18);
        flex: none;
      }
      .count {
        margin-top: 14px;
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
        border: 1px solid var(--edge);
        background: rgba(12, 17, 28, 0.5);
        backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
        -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
      }
      .count > div { padding: 16px 12px 14px; }
      .count > div + div { border-left: 1px solid var(--edge); }
      .count .n {
        font-family: var(--mono);
        font-weight: 500;
        font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 10.4vw, 2.7rem);
        line-height: 1;
        letter-spacing: -0.045em;
        color: var(--glow);
        font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      }
      .count .u {
        margin-top: 9px;
        font-size: 0.65rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.14em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--dim);
      }
      .count.done { display: block; }
      .count.done > div + div { display: none; }
      .count.done .n { font-size: 1.15rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; line-height: 1.4; }
      .count.done .u { display: none; }

      .acts { margin-top: 26px; }

      /* ---------- buttons ---------- */
      .btn {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: 10px;
        width: 100%;
        min-height: 56px;
        padding: 16px 24px;
        border: none;
        border-radius: 3px;
        background: var(--glow);
        color: #241905;
        font-family: var(--sans);
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 1rem;
        cursor: pointer;
        transition: background 0.2s ease, transform 0.14s ease;
        box-shadow: 0 16px 38px -18px rgba(233, 180, 76, 0.95);
      }
      .btn svg { width: 17px; height: 17px; flex: none; }
      .btn:hover { background: #f2c266; transform: translateY(-2px); }
      .btn:active { transform: translateY(0); }
      .btn:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--glow); outline-offset: 3px; }

      /* ---------- sections ---------- */
      .sec { padding-block: 56px; }
      .sec h2 {
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 7.4vw, 2.2rem);
        line-height: 1.15;
        letter-spacing: -0.026em;
        max-width: 19ch;
        text-wrap: balance;
      }
      .sec .lead { margin-top: 16px; color: var(--mut); font-size: 1rem; max-width: 47ch; }

      /* ---------- what changed (散文段) ---------- */
      .changed { background: var(--night-2); border-top: 1px solid var(--edge); }
      .prose { margin-top: 22px; }
      .prose p { color: var(--mut); font-size: 1.01rem; margin-top: 16px; max-width: 50ch; }
      .prose strong { color: var(--stone); font-weight: 600; }
      .datarow {
        margin-top: 30px;
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 10px;
      }
      .datarow span {
        font-family: var(--mono);
        font-size: 0.79rem;
        padding: 8px 13px;
        border: 1px solid var(--edge);
        color: var(--stone-d);
      }
      .datarow span b { color: var(--glow); font-weight: 500; }

      /* ---------- three things ---------- */
      .three { border-top: 1px solid var(--edge); }
      .cards { margin-top: 34px; display: grid; gap: 14px; }
      .card {
        background: var(--slab);
        border: 1px solid var(--edge);
        padding: 26px 22px 28px;
      }
      .card .idx {
        font-family: var(--mono);
        font-size: 0.72rem;
        font-weight: 500;
        letter-spacing: 0.1em;
        color: var(--glow);
      }
      .card h3 {
        margin-top: 12px;
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: 1.24rem;
        line-height: 1.26;
        letter-spacing: -0.018em;
        max-width: 23ch;
      }
      .card p { margin-top: 11px; color: var(--mut); font-size: 0.99rem; }

      /* ---------- two-up (banks vs reits) ---------- */
      .duo { margin-top: 34px; display: grid; gap: 14px; }

      /* ---------- timeline ---------- */
      .day { background: var(--night-2); border-top: 1px solid var(--edge); }
      .slots { margin-top: 34px; }
      .slot {
        list-style: none;
        display: grid;
        gap: 5px;
        padding-block: 22px;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--edge);
      }
      .slot:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--edge); }
      .slot .t {
        font-family: var(--mono);
        font-size: 0.86rem;
        font-weight: 500;
        color: var(--glow);
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      }
      .slot h3 { font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.12rem; letter-spacing: -0.014em; }
      .slot p { color: var(--mut); font-size: 0.97rem; max-width: 46ch; }
      .tz {
        margin-top: 20px;
        font-family: var(--mono);
        font-size: 0.72rem;
        color: var(--dim);
      }

      /* ---------- close ---------- */
      .close { border-top: 1px solid var(--edge); }
      .close .fine {
        margin-top: 17px;
        font-family: var(--mono);
        font-size: 0.72rem;
        color: var(--dim);
      }

      /* ---------- foot ---------- */
      .foot { padding-block: 30px 38px; background: var(--night-2); }
      .foot p { font-size: 0.76rem; color: var(--dim); max-width: 64ch; line-height: 1.6; }

      /* ---------- whatsapp bar ---------- */
      .wa-bar {
        position: fixed;
        left: 0;
        right: 0;
        bottom: 0;
        z-index: 40;
        padding: 12px 22px calc(12px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
        background: rgba(12, 17, 28, 0.9);
        backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
        -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
        border-top: 1px solid var(--edge);
      }
      .wa-btn {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: 10px;
        width: 100%;
        min-height: 56px;
        padding: 15px 22px;
        border: none;
        border-radius: 3px;
        background: var(--wa);
        color: #04210f;
        cursor: pointer;
        font-family: var(--sans);
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 1.02rem;
        box-shadow: 0 12px 30px -14px rgba(37, 211, 102, 0.9);
        transition: background 0.2s ease, transform 0.14s ease;
      }
      .wa-btn svg { width: 22px; height: 22px; flex: none; }
      .wa-btn:hover { background: var(--wa-d); transform: translateY(-2px); }
      .wa-btn:active { transform: translateY(0); }
      .wa-btn:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--glow); outline-offset: 3px; }

      /* ---------- motion ---------- */
      .rise { animation: rise 0.62s cubic-bezier(0.22, 0.72, 0.3, 1) both; }
      .d1 { animation-delay: 0.07s; }
      .d2 { animation-delay: 0.16s; }
      .d3 { animation-delay: 0.26s; }
      @keyframes rise {
        from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(15px); }
        to { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
      }
      .js .reveal {
        opacity: 0;
        transform: translateY(16px);
        transition: opacity 0.55s ease, transform 0.55s cubic-bezier(0.22, 0.72, 0.3, 1);
      }
      .js .reveal.in { opacity: 1; transform: none; }

      /* ---------- larger screens ---------- */
      @media (min-width: 760px) {
        .wrap { max-width: 1060px; margin-inline: auto; padding-inline: clamp(32px, 5vw, 60px); }
        body { padding-bottom: 96px; }

        .hero {
          padding-top: calc(env(safe-area-inset-top) + 80px);
          padding-bottom: 128px;
          background-size: cover, cover;
          background-position: center, center 40%;
        }
        .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 4.4vw, 3.8rem); max-width: 18ch; }
        .hero .lede { font-size: 1.12rem; }
        .count { max-width: 520px; }
        .count > div { padding: 22px 18px 20px; }
        .btn { width: auto; min-width: 260px; }

        .sec { padding-block: 100px; }
        .sec h2 { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 3.2vw, 2.85rem); }

        .changed-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: clamp(40px, 5vw, 72px); align-items: start; }
        .prose { margin-top: 0; }
        .prose p:first-child { margin-top: 0; }

        .cards { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 18px; margin-top: 46px; }
        .card { padding: 32px 28px 34px; }
        .duo { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; margin-top: 46px; }

        .slots { margin-top: 46px; }
        .slot { grid-template-columns: 9rem 1fr; gap: 6px 40px; padding-block: 28px; }
        .slot .t { grid-row: span 2; padding-top: 4px; }
        .slot p { grid-column: 2; }

        .wa-bar { padding-inline: 0; }
        .wa-bar .wrap { display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; }
        .wa-btn { width: auto; min-width: 300px; }
      }

      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        html { scroll-behavior: auto; }
        .rise { animation: none; }
        .js .reveal { opacity: 1; transform: none; transition: none; }
      }
    </style>

    <script is:inline>
      document.documentElement.classList.add('js')
    </script>
  </head>

  <body>
    <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
    <header class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h1 class="rise">
          September just became <span>the Fed meeting that matters</span>
        </h1>

        <p class="lede rise d1">
          US payrolls fell by 23,000 in July against a forecast of 83,000 more. The jobless rate
          dropped to 4.1% anyway. Inflation is still above target. The Fed now has to pick which
          problem to make worse.
        </p>

        <p class="count-label rise d2">Until the Fed decides</p>

        <div class="count rise d2" id="count" data-target={FOMC_AT}>
          <div>
            <p class="n" id="cd-d">{initDays}</p>
            <p class="u">Days</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="n" id="cd-h">{initHours}</p>
            <p class="u">Hours</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="n" id="cd-m">{initMins}</p>
            <p class="u">Minutes</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="acts rise d3">
          <button type="button" class="btn link-btn">
            Get the daily brief, free
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h13M13 6l6 6-6 6" /></svg>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- ============ WHAT CHANGED ============ -->
    <section class="sec changed">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="changed-grid">
          <div>
            <h2 class="reveal">What changed while Singapore was asleep</h2>
            <p class="lead reveal">
              The report came out on Friday evening our time. The US session then spent the rest of
              our night rewriting what it expects from the Fed.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="prose">
            <p class="reveal">
              Normally a falling jobless rate means people found work. This one fell because
              <strong>the labour force shrank</strong>. Give up looking and you're not counted as
              unemployed any more, so the number gets better while nothing actually does.
            </p>
            <p class="reveal">
              Put that next to hiring going backwards and wage growth down to 3.2%, the slowest since
              2021, and you've got a solid case for the Fed to stop. Except inflation hasn't
              cooperated. <strong>Officials were arguing for a hike as recently as last month</strong>,
              and 44% of the market still expects one in September.
            </p>
            <p class="reveal">
              None of this is settled. That's the point. Between now and the decision, the market
              re-bets every time a new number comes out.
            </p>

            <div class="datarow reveal">
              <span>Payrolls <b>−23,000</b></span>
              <span>Forecast <b>+83,000</b></span>
              <span>Jobless rate <b>4.1%</b></span>
              <span>Revisions <b>−103,000</b></span>
              <span>Wage growth <b>3.2%</b></span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ THREE THINGS ============ -->
    <section class="sec three">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="reveal">Three things to get straight before September</h2>

        <div class="cards">
          <article class="card reveal">
            <p class="idx">01</p>
            <h3>Both halves of the job are broken</h3>
            <p>
              The Fed is supposed to keep prices stable and employment full. Inflation says tighten.
              The labour market says stop. There's no setting that fixes both, so whatever comes out
              of September makes one of them worse on purpose.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card reveal">
            <p class="idx">02</p>
            <h3>The market moves before the vote</h3>
            <p>
              Currency and bond markets trade on what they think is coming, not on what's been
              announced. Hike odds went from 57% to 44% in a few hours on Friday. By decision day
              most of the move has already happened, which is why the reaction to the actual news
              often looks backwards.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card reveal">
            <p class="idx">03</p>
            <h3>It reaches your side of the world</h3>
            <p>
              A Washington decision turns up on a Singapore statement within weeks. SORA follows US
              rates, so your floating home loan does too. Your T-bill keeps paying while it lasts.
              The same decision moves both, and they hurt in opposite directions.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ TWO STOCKS, ONE DECISION ============ -->
    <section class="sec three">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="reveal">Same decision, opposite trade</h2>
        <p class="lead reveal">
          Every stock on the SGX is priced off the same number underneath it: what you could earn
          doing nothing. Push that number up and every future dollar of profit is worth less
          today, so the most indebted, longest-duration names get sold first. Hold it, or cut it,
          and the money flows straight back the other way. It's the single biggest lever on this
          index, bigger than any one company's earnings call. The Fed pulls it eight times a year,
          always in the same week.
        </p>

        <div class="duo">
          <article class="card reveal">
            <p class="idx">DBS · OCBC · UOB</p>
            <h3>The 54% of the STI that wants a hold, or a hike</h3>
            <p>
              All three hit record highs in July. Higher-for-longer widens the margin on every
              loan they've already written, and wealth inflows have kept fee income growing
              double digits even as cut talk faded. A September hike doesn't hurt this trade. A
              surprise cut would slow it down — it wouldn't reverse it.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card reveal">
            <p class="idx">S-REITs</p>
            <h3>The side of the index that needs the cut</h3>
            <p>
              Distributions get squeezed every time debt rolls over at a higher rate, and the most
              leveraged names get hit hardest. A hold is a headache. A hike is worse. But this is
              also the side with the furthest to run — the same gearing that hurts on the way up
              turns into the fastest re-rating on the index the moment the cut actually lands.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <p class="lead reveal" style="margin-top:34px">
          This is exactly what the group reads for you, before the vote — which way the incoming
          data is pushing the decision, and which side of that split it favours: stay in the banks
          riding the wider margins, or start building into the REITs everyone else is still
          avoiding, while SGX is still closed and the rest of the market has already re-bet
          without you. This isn't a recap of what the market already did. It's the call that gets
          you there first.
        </p>

        <div class="cards" style="margin-top:34px">
          <article class="card reveal">
            <p class="idx">01</p>
            <h3>We read what moves the odds</h3>
            <p>
              Payrolls, CPI, jobless claims, every Fed speech — the same morning each one lands, in
              plain English, not economist-speak.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="card reveal">
            <p class="idx">02</p>
            <h3>We price the odds, not the headline</h3>
            <p>
              Fed funds futures move on every number before the meeting does. We track where those
              odds sit and translate that straight into "banks" or "REITs," no guesswork required.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="card reveal">
            <p class="idx">03</p>
            <h3>You get it before the open</h3>
            <p>
              Not after. That gap, hours and sometimes days ahead of the crowd, is what separates
              catching the move from reading about it once it's over.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="acts reveal" style="margin-top:30px">
          <button type="button" class="btn link-btn">
            Get the calls before the open
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h13M13 6l6 6-6 6" /></svg>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ ON THE DAY ============ -->
    <section class="sec day">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="reveal">How the day runs, in Singapore hours</h2>
        <p class="lead reveal">
          The decision comes in the middle of our night. This is what the group does with it while
          you sleep.
        </p>

        <ul class="slots">
          <li class="slot reveal">
            <p class="t">2.00am</p>
            <h3>The decision is out</h3>
            <p>
              The rate decision and the statement. The wording usually carries more information than
              the number itself.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li class="slot reveal">
            <p class="t">2.30am</p>
            <h3>The press conference</h3>
            <p>
              Where the next three months actually get set. We flag the lines that moved the market
              and the ones that didn't.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li class="slot reveal">
            <p class="t">7.00am</p>
            <h3>The overnight summary</h3>
            <p>
              What the US session did with it, sitting on your phone before your first kopi.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li class="slot reveal">
            <p class="t">9.00am</p>
            <h3>SGX opens</h3>
            <p>
              Banks and REITs start reacting — in opposite directions. You already know why.
              Everyone else is still working it out.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p class="tz reveal">All times SGT · decision timing follows the Fed's published schedule</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ CLOSE ============ -->
    <section class="sec close">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="reveal">Every number between now and then counts</h2>
        <p class="lead reveal">
          CPI, jobless claims, next month's payrolls. Each one moves the odds again. We follow them
          all the way to the meeting and send three points to the group every trading morning.
        </p>

        <div class="acts reveal">
          <button type="button" class="btn link-btn">
            Join the free WhatsApp group
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h13M13 6l6 6-6 6" /></svg>
          </button>
        </div>

        <p class="fine reveal">Free · nothing to download · leave whenever you like</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="foot">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p>
          Everything here is general market commentary and educational research. It does not take
          your objectives or financial situation into account, and it is not a recommendation to buy
